{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Using the 2021 CKD-EPI Creatinine equation (race-free):\n\nFemale, age 61, creatinine = 5.4 mg/dL.\n\nFor females with Scr > 0.7:\n- κ = 0.7, α = -0.241\n- GFR = 142 × (Scr/κ)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^age × 1.012\n\nScr/κ = 5.4/0.7 = 7.714\n\n(7.714)^(-1.200):\nln(7.714) = 2.0431\n× -1.200 = -2.4517\ne^(-2.4517) = 0.08615\n\n0.9938^61:\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 61 = -0.37937\ne^(-0.37937) = 0.6843\n\nNow multiply:\n142 × 0.08615 = 12.233\n× 0.6843 = 8.371\n× 1.012 = 8.47\n\nFINAL: 8.47"}